    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Using Fermat’s Little Theorem, show that 999 999 is divisible by 7.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$999\\,999=10^6-1\\equiv0\\pmod7$.",
          "worked": "Since 7 is prime and does not divide 10, Fermat’s Little Theorem gives $10^6\\equiv1\\pmod7$.\n$$\\begin{align*}999\\,999&=10^6-1,\\\\999\\,999&\\equiv0\\pmod7.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $999\\,999$ is divisible by 7.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "A number consists solely of the digit 9 and is divisible by 13. Show that it is also divisible by 7 and 11.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The number is divisible by both 7 and 11.\n\nThe powers of 10 modulo 13 have period 6, so the number of digits is a multiple of 6. Then $10^{6k}-1\\equiv0$ modulo both 7 and 11.",
          "worked": "Let the number have $m$ digits, so it is $10^m-1$, where $m$ is a positive integer. The successive powers of 10 satisfy\n$$\\begin{align*}10^1&\\equiv10\\pmod{13},\\\\10^2&\\equiv9\\pmod{13},\\\\10^3&\\equiv12\\pmod{13},\\\\10^4&\\equiv3\\pmod{13},\\\\10^5&\\equiv4\\pmod{13},\\\\10^6&\\equiv1\\pmod{13}.\\end{align*}$$\nThese residues repeat every six powers. Since $13\\mid(10^m-1)$, we have $10^m\\equiv1\\pmod{13}$, so $m=6k$ for a positive integer $k$.\n\nBy Fermat’s Little Theorem, $10^6\\equiv1\\pmod7$. Therefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}10^{6k}-1&=(10^6)^k-1,\\\\10^{6k}-1&\\equiv0\\pmod7.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $10\\equiv-1\\pmod{11}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}10^{6k}-1&\\equiv(-1)^{6k}-1\\pmod{11},\\\\10^{6k}-1&\\equiv0\\pmod{11}.\\end{align*}$$\nHence the number is divisible by both 7 and 11.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100
      }
    ]
  },
